{"findings":[{"rule":"J1","where":"Deployment._configureModules (overrides BaseSetup._configureModules)","severity":"HIGH","why":"The override restricts country 410 instead of 408, so wallet c (registered in country 408 with a valid KYC claim) passes isVerified and the country module's moduleCheck returns true. Tokens can then be sent to a restricted-country investor.","steps":"1. agent.mint(c, 1) or a1.transfer(c, 1). 2. isVerified(c) is true (KYC claim valid). 3. CountryRestrictModule.moduleCheck(c) reads country 408, which is not restricted, so canTransfer passes and the transfer succeeds."},{"rule":"J3","where":"Deployment._configureModules / BaseSetup._restrictCountry","severity":"HIGH","why":"The country module is bound and active, but its restricted-country set is wrong (410 instead of 408). The restriction is therefore not real for the required country.","steps":"1. Setup runs _configureModules, which calls _restrictCountry(410) and never restricts 408. 2. CountryRestrictModule.isCountryRestricted(compliance, 408) returns false."}]}
